+// The stand tie-break: of the tiles a step away in `stands`, which the caller's work takes as equal
+// to here, the one whose own sight (a champion's, radius 8) holds the most by the ward value's
+// weights and bands, if it beats here's and is no less safe by Safety's bound and the camps. Our
+// ward sees the same wherever we stand, so its sight counts for none. `group`, cleared: a hold, every
+// candidate on its camp tiles (any of them keeps it, capture.condition). Else a wait, every candidate
+// off camp tiles or, while `group` respawns after next round's start, on its own (occupation before
+// then does not delay it, capture.respawn). So no step starts or leaves a capture or holds a respawn
+// back. No step with an enemy in sight: there the fight places us.
+inline constexpr std::uint64_t stand_cost = 4000, stand_candidate_cost = 1500;
+[[gnu::noinline]] bool step_for_sight(World& world, Pathing& pathing, Safety& safety, const Memory& memory, const bitboard& stands,
+                                      int group) {
